        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: दुग्धम्",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दुग्धम् (dugdham) — \"milk\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit has two words for milk. You met kṣīram early on; दुग्धम् (dugdham) is the other one, and it is the one the modern languages kept."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It comes from duh, \"to milk\", so दुग्धम् (dugdham) is \"the milked thing\" — the action first, the drink second. Hindi and Gujarati say dūdh, Punjabi duddh, and you can hear the whole word still inside them. Neuter -अम्."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The second word for milk, and the one you would be handed today."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
