        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: मधु",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मधु (madhu) — \"honey\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मधु (madhu) is honey, and sweetness in general."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Almost nothing in this book has cousins this far-flung. English mead is the same word; Greek methu is wine, and amethyst — a-methustos, \"not drunk\" — is the stone that was thought to keep you sober; Lithuanian medus and Old Irish mid are honey and mead again. Even Chinese mì, \"honey\", was borrowed from an early Indo-European neighbour. Ends in short -u, like साधु and दारु."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Honey, and a word that reached from Ireland to China."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
