          "title": "You'll want to know: लवणम्",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "लवणम् (lavaṇam) — \"salt\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "लवणम् (lavaṇam) is salt, and salty as a taste."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Here Sanskrit went its own way: Latin sal and English salt come from a different old word altogether, and लवणम् (lavaṇam) has no cousin among them. It stayed at home instead — lavaṇa still names the salty one among the six tastes of Indian cooking, while everyday Hindi took namak from Persian for the thing in the jar. Neuter -अम्."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Salt, and a word with no European relatives at all."
            }
          ]
        },
