          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: पुस्तकम्",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पुस्तकम् (pustakam) — \"a book\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पुस्तकम् (pustakam) is a traveller. It came into Sanskrit from Persian post, \"hide, skin\" — what a book was written on before paper — and then India handed it back out again."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Hindi pustak, Bengali pustak, Kannada pustaka, Telugu pustakam and Tamil puttakam are all this word. Most of what you have learned here was inherited; this one was borrowed, and you can tell, because its relatives live outside the language rather than inside it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A book, and the one borrowed word in the chapter."
            }
          ]
        },
